Project Design Phase Phase
The design phase explains how the different components of FitBuddy work together.
The application starts with a user input page where the user enters their personal fitness information.
The information is sent to the FastAPI backend.
The backend sends the required fitness information to the Gemini AI model.
Gemini generates a 7-day fitness plan according to the user's goal, fitness level, intensity and available time.
The generated plan and nutrition information are stored in the SQLite database.
The result is then displayed to the user in a simple format.
The user can provide feedback about the plan. The feedback is sent to Gemini along with the original plan, and Gemini generates an updated plan.
The project contains separate pages for the main input page, result page, admin page and user information page.
